; The instruction specification: one description of the ISA, shared by the assembler
; and by the RTL decoder (construction-plan.md section 4, phase_plan.md P1.5).
;
; It sits BELOW both lib/ and model/ and depends on neither. That is the whole reason it
; is its own library: lib/ is installed and model/ is not, so a public RTL module cannot
; depend on a private model one, and two hand-written copies of a field layout is exactly
; the failure P1.5 is asked to prevent. Field positions, opcode numbers and the extension
; rule are written once here; [Encoding.forms] publishes them as data so a decoder can be
; built from the same numbers the assembler encodes with.
;
; Note the absence of `hardcaml`. The specification is bits and their meanings; it holds
; no execution and no circuit. The reference execution model stays in model/, independent
; of the RTL, as construction-plan.md section 4 requires.

(library
 (name protemu_isa)
 (public_name hardcaml_protemu.isa)
 (libraries core)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane))
 (lint
  (pps ppx_js_style)))
